The releases are built without x265, so none of the libraries in them is GPL: libheif and libde265
are LGPL-3.0, which permits static linking but requires satisfying LGPLv3 section 4 (e.g. providing
the object files needed to relink against a modified version of the library, which the source
archive and the static libraries allow); libaom, dav1d, and libwebp are BSD.

If you build with --with-x265, x265 is GPL-2.0-or-later, and GPL has no static-linking exception,
so the resulting archive and everything that links it are a combined GPL work: anyone who
redistributes it must also satisfy the GPL, such as making the corresponding source available and
keeping the GPL notice attached.
